---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Encoding Intent"
  description="Plan first. Prompt second. The methodology behind responsible AI work: human judgment goes in first as structure, standards, and guardrails, then AI builds inside it."
>
  <article class="intent">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="section-cream section" aria-labelledby="ei-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label label-gold">The Methodology</p>
        <h1 id="ei-heading" class="ei-title">Encoding Intent</h1>
        <p class="ei-lede">Plan first. Prompt second. No vibes required.</p>
        <p class="ei-sub">
          Encoding Intent is the discipline underneath every framework here. It
          is how a person stays in control of AI work: not by reviewing every
          line after the fact, but by putting judgment in first, before the
          model writes anything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What it is -->
    <section class="section-dark section" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label intent-label">The Idea</p>
        <h2 id="what-heading" class="ei-section-heading">Judgment goes in first</h2>
        <div class="prose intent-prose">
          <p>
            Before AI writes a single line of code, it needs to understand who
            you are, how you work, what quality looks like, the patterns you
            trust, and the standards you will not compromise.
          </p>
          <p>
            In practice, that means skill files, instruction files, and
            configuration that capture a team's voice, standards, and
            decision-making patterns. The knowledge that lives in people's heads
            gets written down, shared, and made available to AI as context. The
            encoding itself becomes a collaborative act: teams articulate what
            they know, together.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How to apply -->
    <section class="section-cream section" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label label-gold">How to Apply It</p>
        <h2 id="how-heading" class="ei-section-heading">Five steps, in order</h2>
        <ol class="ei-steps">
          <li>
            <strong>Define the structure.</strong>
            Architecture, patterns, boundaries.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Set the standards.</strong>
            Quality bar, testing requirements, style.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Build the infrastructure.</strong>
            CI/CD, validation, governance.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Encode the intent.</strong>
            Skill files, instruction files, configs, guardrails, planning prompts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Then let AI build.</strong>
            Inside the structure, following the intent.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why it matters -->
    <section class="section-dark section" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label intent-label">Why It Works</p>
        <h2 id="why-heading" class="ei-section-heading">The structure holds</h2>
        <div class="prose intent-prose">
          <p class="ei-closing">
            More time in planning and encoding means less time debugging and
            fixing. The human stays in control because the structure holds.
            Speed comes from automation. Direction comes from intent.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="/writing/dispatch-4-encoding-intent-in-practice"
          class="link-light ei-callout"
        >
          See it in practice: how this site was built with 15 skill files and zero vibes.
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related -->
    <section class="section-cream section" aria-labelledby="related-heading">
      <div class="container container-narrow">
        <p class="label label-gold">Part of a Larger Whole</p>
        <h2 id="related-heading" class="ei-section-heading">Where this fits</h2>
        <p class="ei-related-lede">
          Encoding Intent is phase five of <a href="/frameworks/the-lift" class="link">The Lift</a>,
          the point where a team's judgment becomes the environment AI works
          inside. It serves the same mission as everything here:
          <a href="/frameworks/no-human-left-behind" class="link">No Human Left Behind</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .ei-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .ei-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .ei-sub {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
  }

  .ei-section-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .intent-label {
    color: var(--color-gold);
  }

  .ei-steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: ei;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
  }

  .ei-steps li {
    counter-increment: ei;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .ei-steps li::before {
    content: counter(ei);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-gold-dark);
  }

  .ei-closing {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .ei-callout {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .ei-related-lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: var(--max-width-prose);
  }
</style>
